 home—a complex therapy that requires clinical precision, experience, and a deep understanding of autoimmune and neurological conditions. We recognized early on that IVIG administration isn’t one-size-fits-all, and our approach ensures every treatment is individualized, closely monitored, and supportive of long-term health.<br /><br />To maintain the highest standards of care, our nurses receive additional, ongoing training and certifications through the Immunoglobulin National Society (IGNS) and other professional organizations. This ensures that every clinician on our team is current with the latest protocols, safety standards, and patient care practices specific to IVIG.</p>			<h2>Clinical Research Support</h2>							\n				<p>New drug therapies — such as IVIG and other biologics — are developed for highly specialized populations, often requiring precise administration methods. Mobile Medical LA plays a vital role in helping patients access these cutting-edge treatments by facilitating clinical trial participation. Our deep expertise in complex IVIG infusions directly informs our ability to execute clinical trial protocols with accuracy and care, ensuring continuity between investigational research and safe, effective home treatment.</p>','New Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','1234-revision-v1','','','2025-03-31 20:30:29','2025-03-31 20:30:29','',1234,'https://mobilemedicalla.com/?p=1266',0,'revision','',0),(1268,1,'2025-04-01 04:44:39','2025-04-01 04:44:39','<h1>Where Complex Therapies Meet Compassionate Home Care</h1>					<h3>Providing personalized home infusion services and research-ready nursing support across California</h3>					<h2>About Mobile Medical LA</h2>							\n				<p>Founded in 2017 in the heart of Los Angeles, Mobile Medical LA is a vision of expert home health nurses who saw the growing need for in-home care tailored to patients with complex neurological, immunological, and oncological conditions. They understood that patients deserved more 