alth visits—they deserved skilled care delivered with compassion and consistency.</p><p>The name “<strong>Mobile Medical LA</strong>” reflects the company’s mission: bringing high-quality clinical care to the patient, wherever they are. Over time we expanded our services across Southern California, specializing in managing long-term home infusions and supporting patients participating in clinical research.</p><p>We are proud to be <strong>both home health certified and home infusion treatment (HIT) certified</strong> — a distinction that sets us apart in the industry. Being <strong>home health certified</strong> means we meet stringent state and federal standards for providing skilled nursing and therapeutic services in the home setting. Our <em><strong>HIT certification</strong></em> confirms that we are qualified to safely administer complex medications, including biologics and immunoglobulins, with protocols that ensure patient safety and optimal outcomes.</p>			<h2>Specialized in IVIG Infusion Therapy</h2>							\n				<p>Our nurses are specially trained to <strong>administer intravenous immunoglobulin (IVIG) treatments</strong> safely in the home—a complex therapy that requires clinical precision, experience, and a deep understanding of autoimmune and neurological conditions. We recognized early on that IVIG administration isn’t one-size-fits-all, and our approach ensures <strong>every treatment is individualized, closely monitored, and supportive</strong> of long-term health.</p><p>To maintain the highest standards of care, our <strong>nurses receive additional, ongoing training and certifications</strong> through the Immunoglobulin National Society (IGNS) and other professional organizations. This ensures that every clinician on our team is current with the latest protocols, safety standards, and patient care practices specific to IVIG.</p>			<h2>Pioneers in Clinical Research at Home</h2>							\n				<p>New drug therapies — such as IVIG and other biologics — are developed for highly specialized populations, often requiring precise administration methods. Mobile Medical LA plays a vital role in helping patients access these cutting-edge treatments by facilitating clinical trial participation. Our deep expertise in complex IVIG infusions directly informs our ability to execute clinical trial protocols with accuracy and care, ensuring continuity between investigational research and safe, effective home treatment.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">We partner with <strong>principal investigators, contract research organizations (CROs), and the pharmaceutical industry</strong> to deliver investigational drugs directly in the patient’s home. Our nurses are trained in <strong>following clinical trial protocols and regulatory compliance,</strong> allowing research sponsors to conduct reliable studies in a patient’s home—without compromising data integrity or patient safety.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">We believe that bringing research to the home isn’t just about convenience—it’s about expanding access, improving retention, and making breakthroughs possible.</p>','New Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','1234-revision-v1','','','2025-04-01 07:19:42','2025-04-01 07:19:42','',1234,'https://mobilemedicalla.com/?p=1314',0,'revision','',0),(1315,1,'2025-04-01 07:19:43','2025-04-01 07:19:43','<h1>Where Complex Therapies Meet Compassionate Home Care</h1>					<h3>Providing personalized home infusion services and research-ready nursing support across California</h3>					<h2>About Mobile Medical LA</h2>							\n				<p>Founded in 2017 in the heart of Los Angeles, <strong>Mobile Medical LA</strong> is a vision of expert home health nurses who saw the growing need for <strong>in-home care tailored to patients with complex neurological, immunological, and oncological conditions.</strong> They understood that patients deserved more than basic home health visits—they deserved skilled care delivered with compassion and consistency.</p><p>The name “<strong>Mobile Medic