ltr\">We partner with <strong>principal investigators, contract research organizations (CROs), and the pharmaceutical industry</strong> to deliver investigational drugs directly in the patient’s home. Our nurses are trained in <strong>following clinical trial protocols and regulatory compliance,</strong> allowing research sponsors to conduct reliable studies in a patient’s home—without compromising data integrity or patient safety.</p><p dir=\"ltr\">We believe that bringing research to the home isn’t just about convenience—it’s about expanding access, improving retention, and making breakthroughs possible.</p>','New Home','','inherit','closed','closed','','1234-revision-v1','','','2025-04-01 07:36:59','2025-04-01 07:36:59','',1234,'https://mobilemedicalla.com/?p=1319',0,'revision','',0),(1320,1,'2025-04-01 07:36:59','2025-04-01 07:36:59','<h1>Where Complex Therapies Meet Compassionate Home Care</h1>					<h3>Providing personalized home infusion services and research-ready nursing support across California</h3>					<h2>About Mobile Medical LA</h2>							\n				<p>Founded in 2017 in the heart of Los Angeles, <strong>Mobile Medical LA</strong> is a vision of expert home health nurses who saw the growing need for <strong>in-home care tailored to patients with complex neurological, immunological, and oncological conditions.</strong> They understood that patients deserved more than basic home health visits—they deserved skilled care delivered with compassion and consistency.</p><p>The name “<strong>Mobile Medical LA</strong>” reflects the company’s mission: bringing high-quality clinical care to the patient, wherever they are. Over time we expanded our services across Southern California, specializing in managing long-term home infusions and supporting patients participating in clinical research.</p><p>We are proud to be <strong>both home health certified and home infusion treatment (HIT) certified</strong> — a distinction that sets us apart in the industry. Being <strong>h